# WN22-AU-000060: Windows Server 2022 Event Viewer must be protected from unauthorized modification and deletion.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-au-000060-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Event Viewer must be protected from unauthorized modification and deletion.`
    description `Protecting audit information also includes identifying and protecting the tools used to view and manipulate log data. Therefore, protecting audit tools is necessary to prevent unauthorized operation on audit information. Operating systems providing tools to interface with audit information will leverage user permissions and roles identifying the user accessing the tools and the corresponding rights the user enjoys to make access decisions regarding the modification or deletion of audit tools. Sa`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,file-acl,ntfs,ksi-mla-osm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-OSM,NIST-800-53:AU-9`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-OSM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the permissions on the "Eventvwr.exe" file to prevent modification by any groups or accounts other than TrustedInstaller. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement: TrustedInstaller - Full Control Administrators, SYSTEM, Users, ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read & Execute The default location is the "%SystemRoot%\System32" folder.`

    component_id `comp-windows-file-acl`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-OSM by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\System32\Eventvwr.exe does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AU_9 `Windows Server implements AU-9 by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\System32\Eventvwr.exe does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `C:\Windows\System32\Eventvwr.exe`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE exists_check
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_1
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Administrators|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_2
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Administrators|Allow|Modify`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_3
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Administrators|Allow|Write`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_4
        aces string not_contains `NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_5
        aces string not_contains `NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM|Allow|Modify`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_6
        aces string not_contains `NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM|Allow|Write`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_7
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Users|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_8
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Users|Allow|Modify`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_9
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Users|Allow|Write`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_10
        aces string not_contains `Everyone|Allow`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_11
        aces string not_contains `Anonymous|Allow`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_12
        aces string not_contains `Guest|Allow`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF exists_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_4
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_5
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_6
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_7
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_8
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_9
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_10
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_11
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_12
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
